# Architecture

## Overview

<%= projectName %> uses a **<%= template %>** architecture built with **<%= framework %>**.

<% if (template === 'monorepo') { %>
## Monorepo Architecture

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────┐
│         Shared Toolkit              │
│  (cache, database, patterns, etc.)  │
└──────────────┬──────────────────────┘
               │
    ┌──────────┼──────────┐
    ▼          ▼          ▼
┌────────┐ ┌────────┐ ┌────────┐
│Service │ │Service │ │Service │
│   1    │ │   2    │ │   3    │
└────────┘ └────────┘ └────────┘
```

### Benefits
- Shared code and patterns
- Easy dependency management
- Simplified CI/CD
- Atomic commits across services

<% } else if (template === 'microservices') { %>
## Microservices Architecture

```
                ┌──────────────┐
                │ API Gateway  │
                └───────┬──────┘
                        │
        ┌───────────────┼───────────────┐
        ▼               ▼               ▼
┌──────────────┐ ┌──────────────┐ ┌──────────────┐
│   Service A  │ │   Service B  │ │   Service C  │
└──────┬───────┘ └──────┬───────┘ └──────┬───────┘
       │                │                │
       └────────────────┼────────────────┘
                        ▼
              ┌─────────────────┐
              │  Infrastructure │
              │ (DB, Cache, etc)│
              └─────────────────┘
```

### Service Boundaries

Each microservice is independently deployable and owns:
- Its own database schema
- Business logic
- API endpoints
- Tests

